course: dictionary
lesson: 14579
title: Pixy or pixie?
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A pixy is a small magical creature from stories, a bit like a fairy or an elf. Pixies often have pointed ears and pointed hats, and they are known for playing tricks. «The pixies hid Tom's shoes under the bed.» The trick tells you what a pixy does: it plays pranks.
explain: The word can also be spelled pixie, and both spellings mean the same thing. Pixy and pixie are two ways of writing one word, so you only need to learn one meaning.
explain: Look at the clues around a word. «Mia's new pixie cut made her hair very short.» The word hair tells you a pixie cut is a hairstyle, not a knife cut. Pixie cut is informal, which means it is everyday talk rather than the main meaning.
explain: Folk tales from Cornwall and Devon often tell of pixies who lead travellers astray or play tricks on them. When the context is not enough, a dictionary settles it.
fact: A pixy is a small magical creature, like a fairy or an elf.
fact: Pixies often have pointed ears and pointed hats.
fact: Pixie is another spelling of pixy, and it means the same thing.
fact: A pixie cut is an informal name for a very short hairstyle.
fact: In folk tales from Cornwall and Devon, pixies lead people astray or play pranks.
exercise: «The pixy hid behind the mushroom and giggled.» What is a pixy? | A kind of drum | A tall tree in the forest | A farmer's tool | *A small magical creature in stories
exercise: «Mia's new pixie cut made her hair very short.» What is a pixie cut? | *A very short hairstyle | A long plait down the back | A type of pet | A cake with thick icing
exercise: Which word is another way to spell pixy? | fairy | *pixie | elfin | pixel
test: «The pixies played tricks on the farmer all night.» What do the pixies do in this sentence? | *Play pranks | Sell apples at the market | Pay the farmer for his hay | Sleep in the barn
test: «Ben wore a green pixie hat to the party.» What kind of hat is a pixie hat? | A woolly hat for the snow | *A pointed hat, like the ones pixies wear in stories | A tall crown for a king | A flat cap for the rain
exam: Which is true of pixies in stories? | They never play tricks on anyone | *They often have pointed ears | They are always taller than trees | They are big, grey animals that live in the sea
